ean nobody read it.","A link is a read after a write of the same folder by another actor: it shows the reader could have seen the folder, not that it read the content. Folders hold many entries; a name is not a message.","The share above is a floor on what the release shows, counted in folders. It cannot be scaled to the total: OpenAI counts entries and files, not folders, and its 95% figure is a share of Artifactory messaging in the main namespace, which says nothing about how much of that the release samples.","Writers and readers are mostly anonymous runs (one record each). A probable agent is a link by shared rare material with a stated confidence band, not an identity.","Types are read off the folder names by the rules in agenttrace/board.py. A name can fit several; the first rule wins. Redaction masks some digits, so names that look alike may differ."],"sides":{"token":231},"attribution":true}}
